Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 03:46:54 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 08/15] One address for auth + lobby (DW_ADDR); NAT discovery
 can stay on 127.0.0.1

DW_ADDR serves both on one TCP socket, routing a connection to the lobby once
it's authenticated or when its message starts with service 7 (clients only
send even auth request types). Players behind the session tunnel then need
only 127.0.0.1, which also works on macOS. NAT discovery binds only the
sockets it answers from, so DW_STUN_ADDR=127.0.0.1:3074 with
DW_STUN_ALT_ADDR=127.0.0.1:3077 doesn't collide with the game's own ports.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
